# MMBasic is local code

The `picomite-fork/` tree is a git submodule used only as an upstream reference
for MMBasic behaviour, command tables, algorithms, and third-party codecs.

**Do not compile against `picomite-fork/`.** Copy whatever is needed into
`mmbasic/` (interpreter, command implementations, codecs, fonts, tests assets)
and adapt it to Circle / AArch64. Prefer a local, maintainable port over
linking the Pico-specific tree.

Circle (`circle/`) stays a submodule: it is the bare-metal runtime, not the
language implementation.

When a PicoMite file is required, bring it across into `mmbasic/` (or
`mmbasic/third_party/`), strip Pico SDK / hardware includes, and wire it
through the local interpreter. Subsequent work should edit the local copy.
